+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Share a text snippet (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: A caller can submit a snippet and read it back by its link, both as structured data and
+as plain text, with the text byte-identical to what was submitted.
+
+**Independent Test**: Start the service, `POST /pastes` with `{"content": "hello"}`, then `GET` the
+returned `url` and `<url>/raw` — both return the exact original text, and the structured read
+contains no `delete_token`. Delivers a usable sharing tool on its own, with no expiry, revocation,
+or restart behaviour required.
+
+### Tests for User Story 1
+
+> Write these first and confirm they fail before implementing T021–T025.
+
+- [ ] T017 [P] [US1] Create `tests/test_create.py` covering creation and body validation: `POST` with `content` only returns `201` (FR-005); `content` missing → `400`, `content: 5` → `400`, `content: ""` → `201` and stored as empty (FR-006); unknown extra fields are ignored and absent from the read (FR-009); the `201` body has exactly `id`, `delete_token`, and `url == "/pastes/<id>"` (FR-010); a table test over an empty body, invalid JSON, a bare list, a bare number, a bare string, `null`, and `true` → all `400` with nothing created (FR-026, SR-004); and an assertion that every rejection leaves the data directory byte-for-byte unchanged (SR-004). Each test references its FR/SR ids
+- [ ] T018 [US1] Add the size and framing tests to `tests/test_create.py`: `content` encoding to exactly 65 536 bytes → `201` and 65 537 bytes → `413`, including a multi-byte case where the character count is far below the byte count (FR-007, FR-027); a body that is oversized *and* otherwise valid returns `413`, confirming precedence over `400`/`201` (FR-027); a missing `Content-Length` → `400`; `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` → `400`; a `Content-Length` larger than the bytes actually delivered → `400` with no hang (SR-005); and a 50 MB declared body → `413` while the server process's RSS does not grow by the payload size (FR-029, SC-007) (same file as T017 — sequential)
+- [ ] T019 [P] [US1] Create `tests/test_read.py`: `GET /pastes/<id>` returns `200` with `id`, `content`, `created_at`, `expires_at` at their exact values (FR-012); `delete_token` is absent from the body **and** from every response header (FR-013); `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` returns `200`, `Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, and a body byte-equal to the input with no trailing newline and no BOM (FR-014, SR-012); an empty paste returns `200` with `Content-Length: 0`; a fixture containing non-ASCII, emoji, `\n`, `\t`, quotes, and leading/trailing whitespace round-trips byte-identically through both read forms (FR-016, SC-001); storing `<script>alert(1)</script>` and `<html>…` returns them as inert `text/plain`, never `text/html` (SR-012); an id that was never issued returns `404` (FR-028)
+- [ ] T020 [P] [US1] Add the generation and permission tests to `tests/test_security.py`: create 1 000 pastes and assert all ids and tokens are unique, that ids are 22 chars and tokens 43 chars from `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, that ids need no URL encoding (FR-011, SR-001), and that identical content created at different times yields unrelated ids and tokens (SR-001's "not derived from content, time, or a counter"); `os.stat` the data directory and assert mode `0o700` and every record file `0o600`, re-running the creation under a permissive umask of `0o000` to catch a write-then-`chmod` implementation (SR-008)
+
+### Implementation for User Story 1
+
+- [ ] T021 [US1] Add `validate_create_payload(payload)` to `src/pastebin/models.py` implementing rules 4–8 and 11 of the data-model validation table in the exact documented order, each returning a specific message: body decodes as UTF-8 → else `400` `"request body must be valid UTF-8"`; parses as JSON → else `400` `"request body must be a JSON object"`; the parsed value is a `dict` (a list, number, string, `null`, or bool is rejected) → else `400` `"request body must be a JSON object"`; the `content` key is present → else `400` `"content is required"`; `type(payload["content"]) is str` — **`type(...) is str`, never `isinstance`**, so `str` subclasses are rejected → else `400` `"content must be a string"`; and finally `len(content.encode("utf-8")) <= 65536` → else `413` `"content exceeds the maximum size of 65536 bytes"`. Keys other than `content` and `expires_in` are never inspected (FR-009)
+- [ ] T022 [US1] Add the pre-body framing guard to the `POST /pastes` path in `src/pastebin/server.py`, applied **before any body byte is read** (R-06, SR-005, FR-029): `Content-Length` must be present and a non-negative integer → else `400` `"request must declare a valid Content-Length"`; `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` → `400` with the same message; `Content-Length > MAX_BODY_BYTES` (66 560) → `413` `"content exceeds the maximum size of 65536 bytes"` with the body left unread, a `Connection: close` header, and `self.close_connection = True` (an unread body on a reused connection is a request-smuggling hazard); then `self.rfile.read(content_length)` with the validated length, and a short read → `400` `"request body was shorter than the declared Content-Length"`
