+- [ ] T024 [US1] Implement the `GET /pastes/<id>` handler in `src/pastebin/server.py`: look the record up via `store.read_record`, respond `404` `{"error": "not found"}` when it is `None`, otherwise `200` with exactly `{"id", "content", "created_at", "expires_at"}` — `delete_token` is **never** included in the body or any header (FR-012, FR-013, FR-015, SR-009) (depends on T023)
+- [ ] T025 [US1] Implement the `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` handler in `src/pastebin/server.py`: respond `200` with the body `content.encode("utf-8")` written verbatim — no trailing newline, no BOM, no JSON wrapper — `Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, and `Content-Length` computed from the **encoded byte count** never `len(str)` (FR-014, FR-016, SR-012, R-13); failures use the JSON error body even though the success body is plain text (depends on T024)
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 is fully functional and independently testable — the MVP. Run
+`PYTHONPATH=src pytest -q tests/test_create.py tests/test_read.py tests/test_security.py` and
+quickstart Scenario 1.
