+## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Revoke a snippet early (Priority: P3)
+
+**Goal**: The creator can remove a snippet immediately using the secret issued at creation;
+everyone else cannot, and non-existence is always reported in preference to a permission failure.
+
+**Independent Test**: Create a snippet, `DELETE` it with its `X-Delete-Token` and confirm `204`
+then `404` on every subsequent read; separately confirm a wrong token and a missing token both
+return `403` and leave the snippet readable with unchanged content.
+
+### Tests for User Story 3
+
+- [ ] T031 [P] [US3] Create `tests/test_revoke.py`: `DELETE` with the correct token → `204` with an empty body (FR-019); `DELETE` with no `X-Delete-Token` and with a wrong token → `403` `{"error": "invalid delete token"}`, and a subsequent `GET` returns the unchanged content (FR-020, SC-004); a token differing only in its **last character** is rejected (SR-002); `DELETE` of an unknown id and of an expired id, each with a wrong token and with no token — all four return `404` `{"error": "not found"}`, never `403` (FR-021, Edge Case "Both wrong"); after a successful `DELETE`, `GET`, `GET /raw`, and a repeat `DELETE` with the same correct token all return `404` (FR-022); and the token is re-read from the stored record on every request, so no earlier successful read or any client-supplied claim other than the token itself can satisfy the check (SR-006)
+- [ ] T032 [P] [US3] Add the concurrency tests to `tests/test_security.py` for SR-007: spawn N threads issuing the **same** correct `DELETE` and assert exactly one `204`, the rest `404`, and no `403` and no `500` (Edge Case "Concurrent revocation"); spawn concurrent `GET`s while a `DELETE` is in flight and assert every response is either the complete paste or `404`, never truncated or partial (Edge Case "Concurrent reads during revocation"); and add a source-level assertion that `hmac.compare_digest` is used and that no `==` comparison of the delete token exists in `src/pastebin/` (SR-002)
+
+### Implementation for User Story 3
+
+- [ ] T033 [US3] Add a module-level `threading.Lock` and `delete_record(self, paste_id, token)` to `src/pastebin/store.py`, holding the lock across the **entire** read-record → liveness-check → token-compare → `os.unlink` sequence (SR-007, R-09), and returning a three-valued outcome (`NOT_FOUND` / `FORBIDDEN` / `DELETED`); evaluation order is load-bearing — existence and liveness are checked **before** the token, so an unknown or expired id is `NOT_FOUND` regardless of the token supplied (FR-021); the comparison is `hmac.compare_digest(supplied, stored)`, never `==` (SR-002); `FileNotFoundError` from either the read or the `unlink` maps to `NOT_FOUND`; reads deliberately take no lock — `os.replace` and a single `unlink` already give readers all-or-nothing (R-09)
+- [ ] T034 [US3] Implement the `DELETE /pastes/<id>` handler in `src/pastebin/server.py`: read the `X-Delete-Token` header, validate its characters are ASCII before comparing (pre-empting `compare_digest`'s `TypeError` on non-ASCII `str`, SR-004), treat an absent header as an empty token, call `store.delete_record`, and map the outcome to `204` with an empty body and `Content-Length: 0`, `403` `{"error": "invalid delete token"}`, or `404` `{"error": "not found"}` (FR-019, FR-020, FR-021) (depends on T033)
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Stories 1, 2, and 3 are each independently functional. Run quickstart
+Scenario 3.
