+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup — **BLOCKS all user stories**
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Foundational only
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Foundational; extends US1's create/read path
+- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: Depends on Foundational; needs a paste to revoke, so it reuses US1's create
+- **User Story 4 (Phase 6)**: Depends on Foundational; reuses US1's create to have something to persist
+- **Polish (Phase 7)**: Depends on all desired stories being complete
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **US1 (P1)**: No dependency on any other story. This is the MVP.
+- **US2 (P2)**: Independently testable. Touches `models.validate_create_payload`, `store.read_record`, and the `POST` handler that US1 created — so if US1 and US2 are built in parallel by different people they will collide in `models.py` and `server.py`. Sequential delivery (US1 → US2) is the low-friction path.
+- **US3 (P3)**: Independently testable. Adds a new route and a new store method; the only shared edit is the dispatcher row, so it parallelises with US2 cleanly once Foundational is done.
+- **US4 (P4)**: Independently testable. `store.write_record`'s atomic `os.replace` + `fsync` (T006) already delivers most of FR-023, so this phase is mostly the corrupt-record hardening (T037), the startup contract reconciliation (T038), and the tests that prove both.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written first and must fail before the implementation task runs
+- `models.py` validation before `server.py` handlers
+- `store.py` persistence before `server.py` handlers that call it
+- Story complete and its checkpoint validated before moving to the next priority
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- **Phase 1**: T003 runs in parallel with nothing else meaningful (3 small tasks)
+- **Phase 2**: T004 (`models.py`), T005 (`store.py`), T008 (`server.py`), and T011 (`cli.py`) are four different files with no cross-imports at that stage — all four in parallel. Later, T015 and T016 are two different test files, both in parallel.
+- **Phase 3**: T017, T019, and T020 are three different test files — all in parallel. T018 must follow T017 (same file).
+- **Phase 4**: T026 in parallel with nothing else in-phase; T027 follows it (same file).
+- **Phase 5**: T031 and T032 are different files — in parallel.
+- **Phase 6**: T035 and T036 are different files — in parallel.
+- **Phase 7**: T039, T040, and T043 are three different files — all in parallel; T041, T042, T044 are sequential gates.
+- Across stories: once Foundational completes, US3 and US4 can proceed alongside US2 with different developers, given the `server.py` dispatcher is the only shared edit.
