+## Notes
+
+- **[P]** = different files, no dependencies on incomplete tasks
+- **[Story]** label maps a task to a user story for traceability
+- Tests are mandatory here, not optional — SC-008 and Constitution Principle III make an untested requirement an unimplemented one
+- Verify each test fails before implementing against it
+- Commit after each task or logical group
+- Two details are easy to get wrong and are called out verbatim in the task text: `type(x) is int` rather than `isinstance` (because `isinstance(True, int)` is `True`), and `os.open(..., 0o600)` rather than write-then-`chmod` (because `chmod` leaves the window SR-008 forbids)
+- Avoid: adding a `--host` flag (SR-011 forbids the option existing), returning `405` with an `Allow` header (FR-028 requires `404`), logging requests to stdout (FR-003 allows exactly one line), and interpolating input or stored values into error messages (SR-009)